1
00:00:07,844 --> 00:00:09,265
(All characters, places, and organizations
in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:09,290 --> 00:00:10,857
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors, some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:33,651 --> 00:00:35,551
I don't think we've met properly.

4
00:00:37,151 --> 00:00:38,184
No.

5
00:00:48,951 --> 00:00:50,498
Hello, Han Gyu O.

6
00:00:51,398 --> 00:00:53,885
I'm Kim Mu Jin, and as of today
I'm your big brother.

7
00:01:04,184 --> 00:01:06,017
Korea's a democracy,

8
00:01:06,384 --> 00:01:09,851
and in a democracy you can pick any job,

9
00:01:12,544 --> 00:01:14,333
but a host bar escort? Come on.

10
00:01:22,751 --> 00:01:24,651
(Episode 19)

11
00:01:27,810 --> 00:01:31,717
Wipe it off. Wipe the blood off.

12
00:01:37,404 --> 00:01:38,715
Did Han Gyu Seo tell you?

13
00:01:41,836 --> 00:01:42,984
Does that matter?

14
00:01:52,564 --> 00:01:54,706
As long as your big sister
doesn't find out, right?

15
00:01:57,984 --> 00:01:59,333
Gyu Rim doesn't know.

16
00:01:59,526 --> 00:02:02,793
She never will, either. I'll make sure
she never finds out, no matter what.

17
00:02:06,751 --> 00:02:08,251
If she ever finds out,

18
00:02:08,351 --> 00:02:11,451
I'll beat you beyond recognition.

19
00:02:18,484 --> 00:02:19,658
They're written statements.

20
00:02:19,718 --> 00:02:24,271
One from Son Ji Yeol,
one from your host bar manager.

21
00:02:24,572 --> 00:02:27,784
For the record, Son Ji Yeol's
pretty much back to normal.

22
00:02:28,151 --> 00:02:31,951
He's totally fine now.
He even went to Hawaii.

23
00:02:32,984 --> 00:02:35,151
All that talk about a second surgery
was a flat-out lie.

24
00:02:35,251 --> 00:02:37,751
He and his wife and that manager
were all in on it together,

25
00:02:37,751 --> 00:02:40,784
squeezing money out of you
under one excuse after another.

26
00:02:41,084 --> 00:02:43,047
Since I'm sick of saying it out loud,

27
00:02:45,134 --> 00:02:46,721
read it with your own eyes.

28
00:02:51,084 --> 00:02:54,979
Even they couldn't believe
how dumb and clueless you are.

29
00:02:55,351 --> 00:02:57,584
And you're a grown man of 28...

30
00:02:59,651 --> 00:03:03,651
Bled dry for eight years,
and not once did you suspect a thing,

31
00:03:04,184 --> 00:03:05,684
not once did you check.

32
00:03:06,251 --> 00:03:09,651
They said they'd never seen
a sucker like you in their lives.

33
00:03:10,051 --> 00:03:11,583
Is there something wrong with your brain?

34
00:03:11,664 --> 00:03:14,144
Want to go get a cognitive test
or something?

35
00:03:14,551 --> 00:03:18,151
Hey, even if you go now,
you won't find them.

36
00:03:18,184 --> 00:03:20,851
They turned themselves in at the station,
scared you'd beat them to death.

37
00:03:22,951 --> 00:03:27,277
The police will contact you,
so handle everything legally from now on.

38
00:03:33,768 --> 00:03:35,351
Round two is at my place.

39
00:03:38,251 --> 00:03:41,151
Looks like you got beat half to death
somewhere before I even hit you,

40
00:03:41,251 --> 00:03:43,019
so how are you going to walk in
looking like that?

41
00:03:43,044 --> 00:03:44,433
Gyu Rim would faint.

42
00:03:45,684 --> 00:03:49,251
Hey, I'm not letting you go tonight.

43
00:03:50,151 --> 00:03:52,251
You'd pull something stupid for sure.
I can see it coming.

44
00:03:59,484 --> 00:04:03,684
You got hit earlier, so you know
I've still got a decent punch.

45
00:04:05,510 --> 00:04:06,557
So what'll it be?

46
00:04:07,226 --> 00:04:09,219
Another beating first,
or will you just come along?

47
00:05:03,811 --> 00:05:06,715
Who's the scary thug in your room?

48
00:05:08,284 --> 00:05:11,876
Gyu Rim's brother. Not a thug,
and not scary at all.

49
00:05:11,951 --> 00:05:14,951
Just a goofball.

50
00:05:15,584 --> 00:05:19,284
So? Thug, goofball,
Gyu Rim's brother, whatever,

51
00:05:19,384 --> 00:05:22,551
why is he sitting in your room
with murder in his eyes?

52
00:05:22,684 --> 00:05:24,207
Well...

53
00:05:26,301 --> 00:05:27,794
It's a long story.

54
00:05:28,784 --> 00:05:31,996
He's staying here for a while,
so don't go bothering him again.

55
00:05:32,684 --> 00:05:34,751
I'll book you a hotel room.
Want to go stay there?

56
00:05:35,251 --> 00:05:39,628
Is this Gyu Rim's family vacation home?
Their private guest house?

57
00:05:39,684 --> 00:05:43,071
First her son, now her brother,
taking turns on a homestay?

58
00:05:43,177 --> 00:05:44,310
Lower your voice.

59
00:05:46,384 --> 00:05:48,806
Here. Go stay at a hotel.

60
00:05:49,184 --> 00:05:51,813
Why would I go to a hotel
when I have my own place?

61
00:05:56,751 --> 00:05:57,984
Then you...

62
00:05:59,851 --> 00:06:04,384
Tell me the one thing I own
that you want most of all.

63
00:06:04,851 --> 00:06:07,856
Why? You'll give it to me
if I shut my mouth?

64
00:06:08,251 --> 00:06:11,251
Unbelievable. What do you take me for...

65
00:06:11,284 --> 00:06:12,451
Nothing you want?

66
00:06:14,284 --> 00:06:16,546
You really think I'm that kind of...

67
00:06:20,584 --> 00:06:24,684
Those sneakers Stephen Curry wore
winning Game Six of the 2015 NBA Finals,

68
00:06:24,709 --> 00:06:27,942
the ones you flew to New York to bid on.
How much were those again?

69
00:06:30,751 --> 00:06:32,811
- And the second thing you want?
- Nothing.

70
00:06:55,251 --> 00:06:56,651
That cold-hearted girl.

71
00:06:58,184 --> 00:07:01,384
She waited till nobody was home
and cleaned out her stuff.

72
00:07:03,551 --> 00:07:05,151
Not even a "goodbye."

73
00:07:14,351 --> 00:07:18,484
Hardly notice when someone comes in,
but sure notice when they leave...

74
00:07:20,251 --> 00:07:26,078
You know, when I think about
Gyu Yeong never coming home again,

75
00:07:28,351 --> 00:07:31,351
it feels like a hole opened up
right here, Gyu Rim.

76
00:07:31,811 --> 00:07:33,789
The cold wind just whistles through.

77
00:07:36,917 --> 00:07:39,156
She'll call you, at least, Dad.

78
00:07:40,984 --> 00:07:45,151
Even if she calls, I won't answer.
What, you think I have no pride?

79
00:07:46,997 --> 00:07:48,964
I'll just pretend I never had a daughter.

80
00:07:56,484 --> 00:08:02,221
You think she's nothing but happy
after walking out like that?

81
00:08:04,151 --> 00:08:05,715
Cheers.

82
00:08:08,351 --> 00:08:10,951
Thank you for welcoming me,
Father, Mother.

83
00:08:10,951 --> 00:08:15,351
I'll be the sweetest, proudest,
prettiest daughter-in-law in the world.

84
00:08:15,651 --> 00:08:18,651
I'm so happy today.

85
00:08:20,551 --> 00:08:23,484
Mom, Dad, aren't you a little too crazy
about Gyu Yeong?

86
00:08:23,784 --> 00:08:26,784
I'm barely stopping myself
from giving her a piggyback ride.

87
00:08:27,451 --> 00:08:31,684
But, dear, until the renovations
on your new place are done,

88
00:08:32,051 --> 00:08:35,351
you'll be staying here with us.
Won't that be uncomfortable?

89
00:08:35,384 --> 00:08:37,951
Of course it will be. How could it not be?

90
00:08:38,251 --> 00:08:41,951
Not at all. Not one bit.
I actually love it.

91
00:08:41,951 --> 00:08:46,751
Call a girl pretty and look at that,
even her words come out pretty.

92
00:08:47,251 --> 00:08:49,984
What's so good about living with in-laws?

93
00:08:50,651 --> 00:08:53,084
Really. I mean it, Mother.

94
00:08:53,284 --> 00:08:54,684
Your daughter's away studying abroad,

95
00:08:54,717 --> 00:08:57,951
and if Seong Uk moved out too,
you two would be so lonely.

96
00:08:58,151 --> 00:09:02,584
I'll stay until the renovations are done
and be a daughter to you both,

97
00:09:05,251 --> 00:09:10,115
so please be patient with my faults.
I'm in your hands, Mom and Dad.

98
00:09:11,756 --> 00:09:12,984
She said "Mom."

99
00:09:13,251 --> 00:09:16,382
Honey, did you just say "Mom and Dad?"

100
00:09:16,651 --> 00:09:18,915
I'm your daughter from now on,

101
00:09:18,940 --> 00:09:21,249
so I can call you that, right?
Mom and Dad.

102
00:09:21,951 --> 00:09:25,051
That's it. Piggyback ride time. Come here.

103
00:09:25,076 --> 00:09:26,751
- Mother.
- Let me hug you.

104
00:09:29,307 --> 00:09:30,484
Mom.

105
00:09:40,851 --> 00:09:43,898
Bring the ramen over here
when it's done. For my drink.

106
00:09:44,112 --> 00:09:45,359
Put in two eggs.

107
00:09:46,851 --> 00:09:48,330
This one's mine.

108
00:09:48,631 --> 00:09:50,297
Make your own, Dad.

109
00:09:50,451 --> 00:09:53,551
Brat. Why have you been sulking?

110
00:09:54,051 --> 00:09:57,132
Did you tag in for Gyu Yeong
just to nag me?

111
00:10:00,251 --> 00:10:03,808
Why did you cheat?
A man with a wife and kids.

112
00:10:05,284 --> 00:10:08,558
Is cheating all you ever talk about
whenever you look at me?

113
00:10:09,151 --> 00:10:11,251
Can't you see I'm having a hard time
because of Gyu Yeong?

114
00:10:11,251 --> 00:10:14,784
Why would a married man with a family
see another woman?

115
00:10:15,584 --> 00:10:18,151
If you'd never met her,
there'd have been no divorce.

116
00:10:18,751 --> 00:10:21,926
If you'd never met her,
nobody would be hurting now.

117
00:10:22,051 --> 00:10:26,051
Hey, she's still your mother.
What's with "that woman?"

118
00:10:26,084 --> 00:10:28,184
Why did you have to meet her?

119
00:10:28,384 --> 00:10:30,340
Your mother came after me.

120
00:10:30,441 --> 00:10:32,859
They say no tree stays standing
after ten swings of the axe.

121
00:10:32,884 --> 00:10:35,351
Your mother took
more than 50 swings to win me over.

122
00:10:35,351 --> 00:10:36,927
Are you a tree, Dad?

123
00:10:37,194 --> 00:10:39,814
You're a man with reason and common sense.

124
00:10:40,484 --> 00:10:42,351
Then are you a bird?

125
00:10:42,484 --> 00:10:47,751
Saying the same thing over and over.
Are you a parrot?

126
00:10:48,884 --> 00:10:52,851
Every one of my kids is out
to eat their only father alive.

127
00:10:53,851 --> 00:10:55,184
My blood pressure's going up.

128
00:10:56,951 --> 00:11:01,900
Maybe I'm the one who should find
a new family and move out of this dump.

129
00:11:06,851 --> 00:11:07,951
My stomach's burning.

130
00:11:13,651 --> 00:11:18,151
These kids are so petty.
They even ate the tuna I stashed away.

131
00:11:20,084 --> 00:11:21,151
What's this?

132
00:11:23,951 --> 00:11:26,551
What is it?

133
00:11:32,284 --> 00:11:37,431
What is this?

134
00:11:44,851 --> 00:11:47,752
Hey, what's this beautiful lunchbox?

135
00:11:50,805 --> 00:11:52,505
Someone dropped it off for me.

136
00:11:52,530 --> 00:11:55,830
You should've told me sooner
you had something like this. Honestly...

137
00:12:05,151 --> 00:12:06,560
I know this taste.

138
00:12:13,551 --> 00:12:16,629
They put citron in the abalone.

139
00:12:17,863 --> 00:12:20,136
I've definitely tasted this somewhere.

140
00:12:22,951 --> 00:12:28,626
I've got it. Pongdang Restaurant
in Samcheok. This is theirs, right?

141
00:12:28,651 --> 00:12:32,084
This is Ms. Kang's cooking
from Pongdang, isn't it?

142
00:12:33,584 --> 00:12:36,451
No? Then whose is it?

143
00:12:36,984 --> 00:12:43,513
Poksak Restaurant on Jeju Island.
Hanggu Restaurant in Mokpo.

144
00:12:45,984 --> 00:12:48,685
Then Nurungji Restaurant in Busan?

145
00:12:50,552 --> 00:12:51,759
Who, then?

146
00:12:52,951 --> 00:12:54,374
I've had this before...

147
00:13:11,251 --> 00:13:14,358
Gyu Min, Gyu O is staying at my place
for a while.

148
00:13:14,751 --> 00:13:17,251
Come up with something
so Gyu Rim doesn't worry.

149
00:13:18,251 --> 00:13:19,951
Thank you, Mu Jin.

150
00:13:24,284 --> 00:13:25,884
Thank you so much.

151
00:13:43,896 --> 00:13:45,084
I'm coming in.

152
00:14:02,351 --> 00:14:04,705
Why don't you stop thinking
and get some sleep?

153
00:14:10,051 --> 00:14:12,378
There's chamomile tea in the thermos.

154
00:14:13,198 --> 00:14:15,415
Drink it when you can't sleep.
It helps a little.

155
00:14:24,596 --> 00:14:25,616
(Cosmos)

156
00:14:25,641 --> 00:14:26,803
(The Essays of Montaigne)

157
00:14:26,828 --> 00:14:27,943
(Thus Spoke Zarathustra)

158
00:14:34,951 --> 00:14:36,979
Books that put you right to sleep.

159
00:14:37,126 --> 00:14:40,226
Personally, I recommend Nietzsche.

160
00:15:04,751 --> 00:15:08,351
Gyeol left this squishy toy behind.
Take your anger out on it.

161
00:15:08,684 --> 00:15:11,451
Squeeze it as hard as you're angry.
Even better if you wreck it.

162
00:15:12,351 --> 00:15:13,851
I'll just buy Gyeol a new one.

163
00:15:14,684 --> 00:15:18,051
Put all your guilt and hatred
toward yourself into it too.

164
00:15:18,584 --> 00:15:20,551
Beating yourself up is really bad for you.

165
00:15:22,651 --> 00:15:24,251
I did it for eight years. I know.

166
00:15:30,451 --> 00:15:32,858
Son Ji Yeol, the host bar manager,
forget all of it.

167
00:15:32,986 --> 00:15:36,046
I don't know. Let's just sleep.

168
00:15:36,284 --> 00:15:40,035
Think about it after you sleep.
Just close your eyes and sleep.

169
00:15:40,651 --> 00:15:42,394
I'll be keeping watch in the living room,

170
00:15:42,419 --> 00:15:45,419
so don't even dream about
running off or anything.

171
00:17:38,251 --> 00:17:41,268
That woman really is your mother.

172
00:17:41,635 --> 00:17:44,975
She came by before too,
asking if you were Gyu Rim.

173
00:17:45,451 --> 00:17:48,921
But she didn't let on.
She just left the lunchbox and went.

174
00:18:24,884 --> 00:18:27,961
I didn't know you were out here.
I looked all over for you.

175
00:18:31,451 --> 00:18:32,699
Are you all right?

176
00:18:33,720 --> 00:18:36,200
You tossed and turned all last night
without a wink of sleep.

177
00:18:37,384 --> 00:18:39,051
You'll collapse if you keep this up.

178
00:18:44,951 --> 00:18:48,351
Don't worry so much about Seo Hyeon.
She's fine.

179
00:18:48,751 --> 00:18:52,851
I saw her briefly at the office,
and she's holding up just fine.

180
00:18:53,451 --> 00:18:57,903
And did I tell you she left the hotel
and moved in with Ji Hye?

181
00:18:59,351 --> 00:19:04,066
And Jeong Woo is keeping an eye on her,
so don't worry.

182
00:19:04,351 --> 00:19:09,776
I packed a lunchbox for Seo Hyeon
yesterday.

183
00:19:10,751 --> 00:19:11,751
You did?

184
00:19:14,651 --> 00:19:17,323
I took it all the way to her office,

185
00:19:19,649 --> 00:19:24,049
but no matter how long I waited,
she never got back to me...

186
00:19:30,951 --> 00:19:36,651
So I gave that lunchbox to Gyu Rim.

187
00:19:39,951 --> 00:19:41,051
To Gyu Rim?

188
00:19:44,030 --> 00:19:49,564
If Seo Hyeon wouldn't take the food
I made for her, I should've let it go,

189
00:19:51,484 --> 00:19:53,122
but why on earth did I...

190
00:19:55,096 --> 00:19:58,069
Gyu Rim isn't a garbage can
for leftovers...

191
00:20:00,345 --> 00:20:03,336
I went all that way
and couldn't even tell her I'm her mother,

192
00:20:05,484 --> 00:20:11,483
and I just ran off,
afraid she'd recognize me.

193
00:20:15,951 --> 00:20:17,684
What kind of person am I?

194
00:20:18,784 --> 00:20:19,851
Yun Hui.

195
00:20:26,782 --> 00:20:29,151
I don't know what kind of person I am.

196
00:20:30,151 --> 00:20:34,051
Not Seo Hyeon's mother,
and not Gyu Rim's mother either...

197
00:20:37,084 --> 00:20:39,151
What on earth am I?

198
00:20:40,051 --> 00:20:41,884
Why would you think that?

199
00:20:42,451 --> 00:20:46,145
You're Seo Hyeon's mother
and Gyu Rim's mother both.

200
00:20:46,284 --> 00:20:49,351
No matter how much I hated my ex-husband,

201
00:20:49,751 --> 00:20:54,584
those girls were my own flesh and blood.
How could I have gone 17 years,

202
00:20:55,084 --> 00:20:58,984
without a single call,
turning my back that completely...

203
00:20:59,551 --> 00:21:02,705
That's because you wanted to raise
Seo Hyeon right,

204
00:21:03,052 --> 00:21:05,518
to stay devoted to her.

205
00:21:05,951 --> 00:21:08,451
That's why we never gave her
a brother or sister.

206
00:21:09,951 --> 00:21:15,068
I thought that was it,
but I don't think it was.

207
00:21:21,051 --> 00:21:26,684
I matter more to me
than the two of them do,

208
00:21:29,451 --> 00:21:35,751
and the world I'm standing on now
already feels like a sandcastle,

209
00:21:37,351 --> 00:21:40,509
so the thought of them turning up
and tearing it all down,

210
00:21:42,803 --> 00:21:45,123
that must be what terrified me.

211
00:21:53,151 --> 00:21:55,431
I'm terrifying, aren't I?

212
00:21:57,065 --> 00:21:58,979
I'm disgusting, aren't I?

213
00:22:01,384 --> 00:22:04,451
Honey, should we go out for breakfast?

214
00:22:04,491 --> 00:22:09,491
Don't cook. Hotel breakfast is nice.
Let's go to a hotel.

215
00:22:10,584 --> 00:22:11,751
Honey.

216
00:22:13,251 --> 00:22:15,051
Give me some time.

217
00:22:18,430 --> 00:22:23,797
I'm so sorry
I can't even look you in the eye,

218
00:22:28,851 --> 00:22:34,951
but give me some time to think on my own.

219
00:22:39,461 --> 00:22:40,984
What do you mean by that?

220
00:23:03,284 --> 00:23:04,751
That girl, honestly...

221
00:23:09,784 --> 00:23:13,584
Hey, Han Gyu Yeong! Out to ruin me again,
mixing this in with the rest?

222
00:23:13,751 --> 00:23:16,151
I keep telling you,
wash your own clothes...

223
00:23:32,051 --> 00:23:36,243
Fine, Han Gyu Yeong. You said
you tangle up your own life,

224
00:23:38,051 --> 00:23:40,108
so live your life however you want...

225
00:23:42,922 --> 00:23:44,135
Done.

226
00:23:45,951 --> 00:23:51,184
Just like you wanted. You and I end here.

227
00:24:03,851 --> 00:24:07,651
Hey, I woke up this morning
and got the biggest shock.

228
00:24:07,884 --> 00:24:11,084
It wasn't my room in that miserable house.

229
00:24:12,051 --> 00:24:13,951
Yeah.

230
00:24:17,714 --> 00:24:20,827
The housekeeper even brings me
fresh green juice like room service,

231
00:24:21,138 --> 00:24:24,594
and there's a marble bathroom
with a tub right in the room,

232
00:24:25,048 --> 00:24:27,000
and a closet the size of a field.

233
00:24:27,700 --> 00:24:28,700
Hey.

234
00:24:29,050 --> 00:24:33,220
The best part is not having my family
in front of me.

235
00:24:33,431 --> 00:24:35,565
No more hearing those annoying voices,

236
00:24:35,566 --> 00:24:38,150
no more looking at those tired faces.

237
00:24:38,197 --> 00:24:40,277
Se Hui, I'll call you later.

238
00:24:44,673 --> 00:24:47,120
- Why does it look like that?
- Why do you think?

239
00:24:47,396 --> 00:24:49,567
Do you buy clothes
without even checking the size?

240
00:24:50,671 --> 00:24:54,431
They only got one in,
so I grabbed it no matter what.

241
00:24:56,147 --> 00:24:59,725
It looked great on that guy, though.

242
00:24:59,840 --> 00:25:02,859
That guy? What guy?

243
00:25:03,513 --> 00:25:04,888
Are you seeing some guy?

244
00:25:05,381 --> 00:25:06,665
That's not it...

245
00:25:07,005 --> 00:25:08,519
Another guy was about to buy it...

246
00:25:08,520 --> 00:25:09,520
Hold on. You...

247
00:25:09,841 --> 00:25:12,454
Did you mix up my size
with some other guy's?

248
00:25:12,496 --> 00:25:14,412
- Do I look like you?
- Why, you!

249
00:25:15,195 --> 00:25:17,366
Who are you yelling at?

250
00:25:18,707 --> 00:25:20,350
What's with your hand?

251
00:25:20,787 --> 00:25:22,501
Were you about to hit me?

252
00:25:25,842 --> 00:25:27,878
It's tight. I can't breathe.

253
00:25:32,030 --> 00:25:35,023
Do you hit women?

254
00:25:35,847 --> 00:25:37,431
If you ask for it, you get it.

255
00:25:37,498 --> 00:25:43,066
Hey, my dad said women and dried pollack
need a beating every four days.

256
00:25:43,488 --> 00:25:44,746
What?

257
00:25:52,184 --> 00:25:53,433
Why are you hitting me?

258
00:25:53,904 --> 00:25:55,274
What gives you the right to hit me?

259
00:25:55,275 --> 00:25:58,472
Why would you make a call
like that to Se Ra?

260
00:25:59,454 --> 00:26:03,404
Why? Embarrassed?

261
00:26:03,977 --> 00:26:07,319
You old man.
Did you not think of me at all?

262
00:26:12,251 --> 00:26:16,426
I heard you bought Se Ra a necklace.

263
00:26:16,634 --> 00:26:19,875
The same brand as mine,
and the same design!

264
00:26:20,062 --> 00:26:22,599
Why? Afraid you'd get us mixed up?

265
00:26:24,653 --> 00:26:26,655
Be quiet and get inside.
We'll talk inside!

266
00:26:27,880 --> 00:26:29,415
Get inside, my foot.

267
00:26:30,020 --> 00:26:35,416
Gyu Yeong will find out sooner or later
her father-in-law's a legendary womanizer.

268
00:26:35,441 --> 00:26:38,088
Hey! Why, I ought to!

269
00:26:41,721 --> 00:26:44,167
Why hit me? Fine, beat me!

270
00:26:44,734 --> 00:26:46,977
Let's both go down, you jerk.

271
00:26:48,069 --> 00:26:49,752
Hey, let go of me!

272
00:26:49,754 --> 00:26:50,754
Let go!

273
00:26:50,913 --> 00:26:54,207
Who are you texting every night?

274
00:26:54,208 --> 00:26:57,461
Hey, don't you know what privacy is?

275
00:26:57,493 --> 00:26:59,661
- The nerve!
- Why go through my phone?

276
00:27:25,240 --> 00:27:27,022
Looks like he sat up all night like that.

277
00:27:27,439 --> 00:27:31,087
Part samurai, part Joseon swordsman.

278
00:27:34,367 --> 00:27:36,833
His back must not hurt, sitting like that.

279
00:27:37,183 --> 00:27:41,578
His eyes are still shooting lasers
like he'd slice the world in half,

280
00:27:41,580 --> 00:27:43,886
and he's sitting there
with his fists clenched tight,

281
00:27:43,927 --> 00:27:46,460
and if you put a knife in that hand,

282
00:27:50,253 --> 00:27:53,170
he looks like he'd kill someone
and nobody would ever know.

283
00:27:56,953 --> 00:27:59,281
"Hang around a dangerous man,
you get stabbed." Heard that one?

284
00:27:59,434 --> 00:28:01,305
He's dangerous. Extremely dangerous.

285
00:28:01,307 --> 00:28:03,087
My gut's about as sharp
as a fortune teller's, you know.

286
00:28:03,341 --> 00:28:05,912
Make up some excuse
and get him out of this house.

287
00:28:05,914 --> 00:28:07,980
I told you to go stay at a hotel.

288
00:28:08,141 --> 00:28:09,305
Why won't you listen?

289
00:28:09,307 --> 00:28:11,921
How do I run off alone
and leave you in this dangerous house?

290
00:28:11,923 --> 00:28:14,197
I'm telling you,
he's practically a terrorist.

291
00:28:14,454 --> 00:28:15,946
I'm the one holding the knife.

292
00:28:16,107 --> 00:28:17,687
- Do I not look dangerous?
- What?

293
00:28:18,140 --> 00:28:19,667
Slander that goofball one more time...

294
00:28:20,520 --> 00:28:22,440
Gyu O, I mean. Just try it,

295
00:28:22,781 --> 00:28:24,610
and this knife won't only slice onions.

296
00:28:24,730 --> 00:28:26,688
So two more words about Gyu O,
that goofball...

297
00:28:27,476 --> 00:28:29,160
Then you'll kill me?

298
00:28:31,887 --> 00:28:35,796
Once you go crazy over love,
friendship means nothing at all.

299
00:28:36,693 --> 00:28:39,182
Fifteen years of friendship, worthless.

300
00:28:39,561 --> 00:28:42,170
Because of that damn family selfishness,

301
00:28:42,351 --> 00:28:44,297
this country can't make the G7.

302
00:28:52,432 --> 00:28:53,513
It's good.

303
00:28:56,634 --> 00:28:57,634
So annoying.

304
00:29:18,075 --> 00:29:19,593
Did you sit up all night like this?

305
00:29:22,527 --> 00:29:23,693
Doesn't your back hurt?

306
00:29:25,681 --> 00:29:29,002
I doubt you want to eat
sitting across from me,

307
00:29:30,785 --> 00:29:32,917
so the kimchi stew is on the stove,

308
00:29:33,050 --> 00:29:34,597
the rice is in the cooker,

309
00:29:34,745 --> 00:29:36,320
and the side dishes are in the fridge.

310
00:29:37,114 --> 00:29:38,360
Just help yourself.

311
00:29:50,093 --> 00:29:51,554
You're scared of yourself too, aren't you?

312
00:29:56,022 --> 00:29:59,236
That's why you're just sitting there
without moving, isn't it?

313
00:29:59,892 --> 00:30:03,174
Because if you blow up again here,
there's no fixing it.

314
00:30:03,614 --> 00:30:05,278
And Gyu Rim would find out.

315
00:30:06,660 --> 00:30:07,660
That's a relief.

316
00:30:07,935 --> 00:30:09,566
You and I are headed to the same place.

317
00:30:12,294 --> 00:30:14,433
Gyu Rim not crying anymore.

318
00:30:15,560 --> 00:30:18,343
Gyu Rim not getting hurt anymore.

319
00:30:24,516 --> 00:30:28,094
Let's not go off route.
Let's make it all the way there.

320
00:30:28,813 --> 00:30:32,080
Once we get to that destination,

321
00:30:32,910 --> 00:30:34,287
I'll give you a proper apology
for hitting you yesterday.

322
00:30:54,541 --> 00:30:57,487
The call cannot be connected
and will go to voicemail...

323
00:30:59,326 --> 00:31:00,755
That girl Gyu Yeong, honestly...

324
00:31:01,086 --> 00:31:02,586
Won't answer calls, won't read texts.

325
00:31:03,400 --> 00:31:06,669
Cold as ice, the spitting image
of her mother.

326
00:31:08,872 --> 00:31:11,965
Fine. Let's say she doesn't exist.

327
00:31:11,990 --> 00:31:14,150
I have two sons and two daughters.

328
00:31:14,348 --> 00:31:16,290
Two boys, two girls. Those are my kids.

329
00:31:18,914 --> 00:31:21,340
Are you giving this radish kimchi
to that punk too?

330
00:31:23,574 --> 00:31:26,894
That knockoff. That guy in sweats.

331
00:31:27,373 --> 00:31:28,572
No.

332
00:31:31,861 --> 00:31:33,647
What's the address of his restaurant?

333
00:31:34,301 --> 00:31:36,081
I think I need to see it with my own eyes.

334
00:31:36,082 --> 00:31:38,019
Why would you go there, Dad?

335
00:31:38,021 --> 00:31:41,478
He might become my son-in-law.
Shouldn't I check him out properly?

336
00:31:41,621 --> 00:31:44,416
How big the restaurant is,
what the revenue looks like.

337
00:31:44,441 --> 00:31:46,567
There's nothing between him and me.

338
00:31:46,907 --> 00:31:49,878
He's never going to be your son-in-law,
so don't get carried away.

339
00:31:51,127 --> 00:31:53,386
He said he likes you.

340
00:31:53,673 --> 00:31:55,943
And I hear you and Gyeol like him too.

341
00:31:56,114 --> 00:31:57,438
No.

342
00:31:57,548 --> 00:32:00,260
That was before. Not now.

343
00:32:00,687 --> 00:32:02,939
He has nothing to do with me.

344
00:32:06,343 --> 00:32:09,260
He's not a married man, is he?

345
00:32:09,285 --> 00:32:10,325
Dad!

346
00:32:10,854 --> 00:32:12,567
Why are you shouting?

347
00:32:12,601 --> 00:32:14,546
Am I the easy target?

348
00:32:14,766 --> 00:32:16,373
I have no money, no job,

349
00:32:16,516 --> 00:32:18,503
so every last person looks down on me,

350
00:32:18,684 --> 00:32:21,867
but I'm still the father
who put you all on this earth.

351
00:32:22,287 --> 00:32:24,300
I'm so hurt, I really am.

352
00:32:25,613 --> 00:32:27,860
Your spit got all over the radish kimchi.

353
00:32:28,153 --> 00:32:30,626
Your spit is in it,
so you eat the whole thing.

354
00:32:32,503 --> 00:32:33,740
How am I supposed to eat all this?

355
00:32:36,507 --> 00:32:37,507
Hey.

356
00:32:40,307 --> 00:32:41,711
How am I supposed to finish all this?

357
00:32:49,107 --> 00:32:50,107
Hello.

358
00:32:53,774 --> 00:32:56,772
This is cocoa. I bought way too much.

359
00:32:57,480 --> 00:32:58,480
Let's split it.

360
00:32:59,506 --> 00:33:01,908
I have money for cocoa too.

361
00:33:02,373 --> 00:33:04,180
I told you, I bought too much.

362
00:33:06,160 --> 00:33:07,912
So if I drink all of this myself,

363
00:33:07,980 --> 00:33:10,340
and get a blood sugar spike,
will you take responsibility?

364
00:33:13,001 --> 00:33:14,001
Fine.

365
00:33:14,103 --> 00:33:17,407
Then I'll take it all home
and drink 30 cups a day.

366
00:33:17,636 --> 00:33:21,193
You don't care if I get diabetes, do you?

367
00:33:24,730 --> 00:33:29,146
I'm not coming to you.

368
00:33:31,438 --> 00:33:34,531
I never will.

369
00:33:36,907 --> 00:33:38,647
So let's stop this, Mu Jin.

370
00:33:40,107 --> 00:33:41,508
They're never kind words,

371
00:33:42,002 --> 00:33:44,827
always mean words, hurtful words.

372
00:33:46,246 --> 00:33:47,886
I want to stop too.

373
00:33:49,354 --> 00:33:51,476
Let me off the hook, Mu Jin. Please.

374
00:33:52,814 --> 00:33:55,130
- No.
- Mu Jin.

375
00:33:55,155 --> 00:33:58,955
Say all the mean, painful,
hurtful words you want.

376
00:34:00,413 --> 00:34:02,360
Just don't let your own words
be the ones that hurt you.

377
00:34:05,527 --> 00:34:07,965
I wanted to look at you a long time today,

378
00:34:08,590 --> 00:34:10,124
so I put in some effort before I came out.

379
00:34:11,526 --> 00:34:14,860
Can't you look at me a little kindly,
just for the effort?

380
00:34:15,938 --> 00:34:17,300
Even for just five minutes.

381
00:34:29,433 --> 00:34:31,496
If you think I'm going to get tired,

382
00:34:31,808 --> 00:34:33,360
you'd better let that go.

383
00:34:34,321 --> 00:34:36,268
Shot down every day
and I come back every day.

384
00:34:39,520 --> 00:34:42,555
I'm never losing you again like an idiot.

385
00:35:06,607 --> 00:35:08,499
Hi, Su Nam. You called?

386
00:35:08,872 --> 00:35:11,417
I was in class and couldn't answer.
I'm sorry.

387
00:35:11,442 --> 00:35:15,046
Hui Na, I heard you're seeing
some lowlife these days.

388
00:35:15,103 --> 00:35:16,207
A lowlife?

389
00:35:18,913 --> 00:35:20,039
Me, seeing a lowlife?

390
00:35:20,176 --> 00:35:22,074
Don't even think about denying it.

391
00:35:22,401 --> 00:35:25,038
I heard it straight from Gyu O.

392
00:35:25,272 --> 00:35:27,813
So warm.

393
00:35:28,773 --> 00:35:31,403
Feels like my blood circulates on its own.

394
00:35:35,319 --> 00:35:37,156
Did Gyu O really say that?

395
00:35:37,794 --> 00:35:39,747
That I'm seeing a lowlife?

396
00:35:39,772 --> 00:35:40,991
That's what he said.

397
00:35:41,461 --> 00:35:44,195
There's some damn fool,

398
00:35:44,347 --> 00:35:49,034
who doesn't know his place
and is crazy about you, Hui Na.

399
00:35:49,226 --> 00:35:51,959
And I hear you've fallen hard for him too.

400
00:35:52,401 --> 00:35:54,659
He said I should call your parents in,

401
00:35:54,661 --> 00:35:57,175
give that lowlife a good scolding,

402
00:35:57,177 --> 00:35:59,980
and split the two of you up.
So what should I do?

403
00:36:00,867 --> 00:36:05,426
Should I share this huge news
with your parents?

404
00:36:05,514 --> 00:36:06,723
No.

405
00:36:06,884 --> 00:36:10,040
Han Gyu O doesn't know anything.
He got it wrong.

406
00:36:10,813 --> 00:36:13,551
The person I'm seeing isn't a lowlife.

407
00:36:13,605 --> 00:36:16,233
He's a really great, kind,
good man, Su Nam.

408
00:36:16,258 --> 00:36:20,154
- Hey, turn the heat up higher.
- Yes.

409
00:36:22,515 --> 00:36:25,707
That's nice.

410
00:36:26,253 --> 00:36:30,233
My muscles are loosening up
and my whole body's melting.

411
00:36:31,207 --> 00:36:32,902
Where was I?

412
00:36:33,248 --> 00:36:37,449
Anyway, never mind.
Before I call your parents,

413
00:36:37,474 --> 00:36:40,759
break up with that total lowlife
right now.

414
00:36:41,080 --> 00:36:43,038
I told you, he's not a lowlife.

415
00:36:43,651 --> 00:36:45,992
You'd like him too if you met him.

416
00:36:46,250 --> 00:36:49,457
You said it yourself before.
You'd vouch...

417
00:36:52,987 --> 00:36:55,775
Anyway, I can't tell you right now,

418
00:36:56,629 --> 00:36:58,467
so just wait a little.

419
00:36:58,867 --> 00:37:00,615
If you give me a little time...

420
00:37:00,640 --> 00:37:04,960
You've already got blinders on,
haven't you?

421
00:37:05,467 --> 00:37:08,606
I'll either call your parents
or step in myself.

422
00:37:08,631 --> 00:37:09,991
Su Nam.

423
00:37:10,487 --> 00:37:13,539
If you absolutely have to date someone,

424
00:37:13,628 --> 00:37:17,607
forget the wrong guy
and see Gyu O instead.

425
00:37:18,476 --> 00:37:19,840
Gyu O?

426
00:37:21,407 --> 00:37:25,429
- What? It's over already?
- Yes, it's done.

427
00:37:25,507 --> 00:37:27,563
Could you do it one more time?

428
00:37:28,327 --> 00:37:31,448
It feels so good I don't want to get up.

429
00:37:31,567 --> 00:37:33,094
Yes, of course.

430
00:37:33,423 --> 00:37:34,634
Thank you.

431
00:37:34,750 --> 00:37:37,512
You don't like Gyu O?

432
00:37:38,434 --> 00:37:41,426
You just don't know Gyu O very well.

433
00:37:41,851 --> 00:37:44,455
He may not have a decent job yet,

434
00:37:44,481 --> 00:37:47,715
but he can always find a job,

435
00:37:48,015 --> 00:37:52,860
and he'll never let you go hungry, Hui Na.

436
00:37:53,044 --> 00:37:56,696
He's young but thoughtful, hardworking,

437
00:37:56,721 --> 00:37:59,827
kind, and respectful to his elders.

438
00:38:00,147 --> 00:38:02,511
Compared to that total lowlife
you're seeing,

439
00:38:02,536 --> 00:38:06,618
he's a hundred, a thousand times better.

440
00:38:07,787 --> 00:38:10,068
I told you before.

441
00:38:10,220 --> 00:38:14,218
After my Heung Sik,
he's the one I'd vouch for.

442
00:38:14,860 --> 00:38:16,751
Yes, you did.

443
00:38:17,300 --> 00:38:21,796
You said I could relax
since you vouched for him.

444
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:25,537
I've matched up five couples,

445
00:38:26,331 --> 00:38:29,058
and they had pretty little babies,

446
00:38:29,059 --> 00:38:32,193
and every one of them is living well.

447
00:38:32,634 --> 00:38:33,765
All right, Su Nam.

448
00:38:34,059 --> 00:38:36,513
I'll break up with that lowlife
right away,

449
00:38:36,716 --> 00:38:40,307
so please match me up with Han Gyu O.

450
00:38:43,327 --> 00:38:47,780
Good thinking. Don't you worry.

451
00:38:48,187 --> 00:38:49,920
Thank you, Su Nam.

452
00:38:56,082 --> 00:39:00,371
Lying here in paradise,

453
00:39:00,396 --> 00:39:04,418
I just saved a girl
who was headed for ruin.

454
00:39:06,146 --> 00:39:09,776
Your nephew. I mean, my boss.

455
00:39:10,522 --> 00:39:14,937
He said he's moving to the States
for his kids. Is that confirmed?

456
00:39:14,962 --> 00:39:16,417
Yes, he's going.

457
00:39:17,458 --> 00:39:22,366
So I'm going to take over
this store myself.

458
00:39:24,694 --> 00:39:28,754
How could I hand over a place this good
to someone else?

459
00:39:29,707 --> 00:39:31,460
Stay with me to the end.

460
00:39:31,485 --> 00:39:34,880
Help me out.
Let's do this together, Ms. Song.

461
00:39:35,787 --> 00:39:37,780
Yes, ma'am.

462
00:39:43,027 --> 00:39:48,592
Han Gyu O, what were you thinking,
trying to tattle to my parents?

463
00:39:50,401 --> 00:39:51,948
Honestly...

464
00:40:03,518 --> 00:40:05,732
(Kwon Hui Na)

465
00:40:16,540 --> 00:40:19,494
The call cannot be connected
and will go to voicemail...

466
00:40:19,519 --> 00:40:21,002
Why isn't he answering?

467
00:40:26,687 --> 00:40:28,040
The unread mark won't go away.

468
00:40:34,334 --> 00:40:37,215
Not answering calls, not reading texts.

469
00:40:38,596 --> 00:40:39,777
Are you sick?

470
00:40:39,981 --> 00:40:41,654
Nothing's wrong, is it?

471
00:40:44,266 --> 00:40:46,660
I'm worried sick, so call me back soon.

472
00:40:48,819 --> 00:40:51,913
And you and I seem to be fated
no matter what we do,

473
00:40:52,150 --> 00:40:54,268
so give up and surrender, Han Gyu O!

474
00:41:14,853 --> 00:41:17,322
- It's sticking because of you.
- Not my fault.

475
00:41:17,347 --> 00:41:18,812
Thanks, Gyu Seo.

476
00:41:21,688 --> 00:41:23,146
This is so good.

477
00:41:32,834 --> 00:41:35,087
- What's that?
- What do you think?

478
00:41:38,020 --> 00:41:40,141
Ha Ye Won, Lee Ho Jin, Gong Su Jeong,
Lim Mi Na, Shin Ye Seul,

479
00:41:40,166 --> 00:41:41,888
Han Yi Seon, Kim Chae Won,
Moon Jae Hun, Cho...

480
00:41:44,086 --> 00:41:45,148
You got the text, right?

481
00:41:49,013 --> 00:41:50,013
What is this?

482
00:41:50,441 --> 00:41:52,816
The names of the kids who told me
to bring you this.

483
00:41:52,841 --> 00:41:54,251
Am I your errand boy?

484
00:41:54,376 --> 00:41:55,713
You should've said no.

485
00:41:55,714 --> 00:41:57,094
Why go to the trouble of hauling it over?

486
00:41:57,467 --> 00:41:59,700
I just handed out a pile this big
to the other kids.

487
00:41:59,894 --> 00:42:02,767
Sure. Aren't you something.

488
00:42:06,014 --> 00:42:08,267
Come outside a second.
I need to talk to you.

489
00:42:08,954 --> 00:42:11,420
Me too. I have something to tell you.

490
00:42:14,771 --> 00:42:16,107
What is it?

491
00:42:16,147 --> 00:42:17,421
- You first.
- You first.

492
00:42:17,461 --> 00:42:18,834
You're the older one, so you first.

493
00:42:18,835 --> 00:42:20,648
You brought it up, so you first.

494
00:42:21,159 --> 00:42:23,826
Fine. Let's say it at the same time.

495
00:42:24,961 --> 00:42:27,342
Three, two, one.

496
00:42:27,367 --> 00:42:28,820
- You're hiding something from me.
- You're hiding something from me.

497
00:42:29,538 --> 00:42:30,824
- What is it?
- What is it?

498
00:42:30,849 --> 00:42:32,282
- Don't even try to lie.
- Don't even try to lie.

499
00:42:34,268 --> 00:42:36,704
Fine. I'll go first.

500
00:42:36,729 --> 00:42:37,815
No, me first.

501
00:42:38,014 --> 00:42:40,155
Fine. You go first, then.

502
00:42:42,396 --> 00:42:43,614
No, you go first.

503
00:42:44,054 --> 00:42:45,627
Then let's say that at the same time too.

504
00:42:46,114 --> 00:42:48,252
Three, two, one.

505
00:42:48,253 --> 00:42:50,152
- I told Mu Jin everything about Gyu O.
- I met Gyu Rim's birth mother.

506
00:42:50,154 --> 00:42:51,374
I got her number too.

507
00:42:51,654 --> 00:42:53,516
You met Gyu Rim's birth mother?

508
00:42:53,823 --> 00:42:55,094
You even got her number?

509
00:42:55,214 --> 00:42:57,155
You told Mu Jin about Gyu O?

510
00:42:57,583 --> 00:42:58,827
How much did you tell him?

511
00:43:06,460 --> 00:43:10,387
She didn't even tell Gyu Rim
that she's her mother?

512
00:43:10,602 --> 00:43:12,405
After going all that way? Why?

513
00:43:13,504 --> 00:43:14,906
I don't know about that,

514
00:43:15,481 --> 00:43:18,054
but it looked like she remarried
and has a family of her own.

515
00:43:18,926 --> 00:43:21,801
He threw away a wife that beautiful
for a woman who looks like a demon...

516
00:43:22,294 --> 00:43:23,720
Has Dad really lost his mind?

517
00:43:23,834 --> 00:43:26,287
How do you know she looks like a demon?

518
00:43:26,527 --> 00:43:27,998
You don't even know her face.

519
00:43:28,001 --> 00:43:30,047
What mother? That woman is no mother.

520
00:43:30,674 --> 00:43:33,771
When you were little, you ran off
looking for her and made a scene,

521
00:43:33,898 --> 00:43:36,359
and do you know how hard
that was on Gyu Rim?

522
00:43:36,384 --> 00:43:38,358
Me? When?

523
00:43:39,767 --> 00:43:41,038
I never did that.

524
00:43:41,393 --> 00:43:43,817
Fine. That's the end of that.

525
00:43:45,061 --> 00:43:48,371
So did you tell Gyu Rim's mother
your name was Han Gyu Seo?

526
00:43:50,196 --> 00:43:53,534
No. I lied and said Kim Gyu Seo.

527
00:43:53,674 --> 00:43:56,711
Afraid she'd know who you were
if you said Han Gyu Seo?

528
00:43:56,892 --> 00:43:58,122
If she found out, she'd be like...

529
00:44:01,447 --> 00:44:03,367
"So you're that woman's son."

530
00:44:03,501 --> 00:44:05,128
"You rotten little brat."

531
00:44:05,427 --> 00:44:08,388
"You're dead today."
Afraid she'd curse you out and hit you?

532
00:44:10,287 --> 00:44:13,024
Why did you tell Mu Jin about Gyu O?

533
00:44:14,748 --> 00:44:15,986
I don't know either.

534
00:44:16,221 --> 00:44:19,519
Mu Jin caught me crying over Gyu O.

535
00:44:19,834 --> 00:44:22,083
So he caught you. Why tell him everything?

536
00:44:24,087 --> 00:44:27,844
When the sun is that warm,
how does a traveler keep his coat on?

537
00:44:28,420 --> 00:44:29,556
What's that supposed to mean?

538
00:44:29,680 --> 00:44:33,347
I mean Mu Jin is that solid and warm.

539
00:44:33,414 --> 00:44:36,000
It all just came pouring out
before I knew it.

540
00:44:36,071 --> 00:44:39,351
You know, if nothing else,
I can really keep a secret.

541
00:44:39,514 --> 00:44:41,874
Even I was shocked after I said it all.

542
00:44:43,443 --> 00:44:44,947
Think back to when we were kids.

543
00:44:45,008 --> 00:44:47,045
What would we have done without Mu Jin?

544
00:44:47,854 --> 00:44:52,100
Mu Jin feels like family to me now,
like a big brother.

545
00:44:52,348 --> 00:44:54,220
Like a guardian over our whole family.

546
00:44:55,313 --> 00:44:58,381
So is Gyu O at Mu Jin's place right now?

547
00:44:58,668 --> 00:45:00,501
And you told Gyu Rim he went on a trip?

548
00:45:12,853 --> 00:45:14,635
If you ask for it, you get it.

549
00:45:15,813 --> 00:45:19,595
My dad said women and dried pollack
need a beating every four days.

550
00:45:22,953 --> 00:45:25,440
Let's both go down, you jerk!

551
00:45:26,373 --> 00:45:28,982
Hey, let go of me! Let go!

552
00:45:29,007 --> 00:45:32,262
Who's the guy you text every night?

553
00:45:32,287 --> 00:45:35,767
Hey, don't you know what privacy is?

554
00:45:35,792 --> 00:45:38,099
- The nerve!
- Why go through my phone?

555
00:45:47,440 --> 00:45:50,733
Order 15, your iced americano is ready.

556
00:45:50,758 --> 00:45:51,791
Yes.

557
00:45:56,974 --> 00:45:58,161
Thank you.

558
00:45:58,313 --> 00:46:00,453
Right.

559
00:46:02,940 --> 00:46:08,179
Sorry, it's a shame, but I don't think
I can make Milan this time.

560
00:46:09,027 --> 00:46:14,262
All right, but I'll make it to Paris
instead, no matter what.

561
00:46:16,793 --> 00:46:20,773
Right, it's about time for my guest...

562
00:46:21,146 --> 00:46:22,726
Let's talk again.

563
00:46:23,058 --> 00:46:24,678
Have a good day!

564
00:46:28,120 --> 00:46:29,227
You're here?

565
00:46:29,753 --> 00:46:33,700
What's this ancient routine now?

566
00:46:34,068 --> 00:46:35,681
I knew you'd bring it back.

567
00:46:35,967 --> 00:46:38,938
Would a size that fits me fit Seong Uk?

568
00:46:40,301 --> 00:46:42,292
Weren't we supposed to meet at 3 p.m.?

569
00:46:42,434 --> 00:46:43,774
Do you have another appointment
besides me?

570
00:46:43,799 --> 00:46:46,239
No, I don't have another one.

571
00:46:46,500 --> 00:46:49,440
No. I think you got the time wrong.

572
00:46:50,752 --> 00:46:54,640
Were you planning to pick up women here?
Should I move?

573
00:46:54,665 --> 00:46:57,955
What are you on about?
Just hand the clothes back over.

574
00:46:59,162 --> 00:47:02,113
Flirting by reciting foreign words
you don't even understand,

575
00:47:02,138 --> 00:47:05,424
that's a Paleolithic move, Cho Heung Sik.

576
00:47:05,924 --> 00:47:08,274
With taste that cheap and outdated,

577
00:47:08,900 --> 00:47:10,838
are you trying to pick up a cavewoman?

578
00:47:11,427 --> 00:47:15,107
Save the nonsense for your own house,

579
00:47:15,200 --> 00:47:17,054
and hand over the shopping bag.

580
00:47:19,047 --> 00:47:24,009
What you want is one thing.
What you can do is another.

581
00:47:24,034 --> 00:47:25,841
If you want to be happy,

582
00:47:25,919 --> 00:47:29,237
live by doing what you can, please!

583
00:47:31,233 --> 00:47:32,854
Should I translate that for you?

584
00:47:37,126 --> 00:47:38,319
Right...

585
00:47:38,793 --> 00:47:40,160
You're right.

586
00:47:41,079 --> 00:47:43,819
Wanting something doesn't mean
you can have it,

587
00:47:44,045 --> 00:47:48,718
and having it all doesn't make you happy.

588
00:47:49,804 --> 00:47:51,039
But...

589
00:47:51,541 --> 00:47:54,056
When are you going to grow up?

590
00:47:59,994 --> 00:48:02,599
If I sit with a married woman too long,
people will get the wrong idea.

591
00:48:02,666 --> 00:48:03,700
I'm off.

592
00:48:09,407 --> 00:48:12,777
And my mother met your mother,

593
00:48:13,077 --> 00:48:15,878
and said she was cold, chilly,
and heartless,

594
00:48:16,083 --> 00:48:19,879
the spitting image of you.

595
00:48:20,013 --> 00:48:22,307
So is your meanness genetic?

596
00:48:22,332 --> 00:48:23,605
What do you mean by that?

597
00:48:23,726 --> 00:48:25,294
Where did she see my mother?

598
00:48:27,172 --> 00:48:28,767
Where did she see her?

599
00:48:36,534 --> 00:48:40,694
(Suragan Side Dishes)

600
00:48:42,781 --> 00:48:44,375
Why did Mom come to see you?

601
00:48:46,227 --> 00:48:48,393
Why would she come to you?

602
00:48:48,947 --> 00:48:50,713
She was so cold to me,

603
00:48:50,738 --> 00:48:52,812
so why did she come to you?

604
00:48:53,066 --> 00:48:54,299
What did she say?

605
00:48:54,425 --> 00:48:56,956
She saw the shabby way you live
and offered you money, didn't she?

606
00:48:56,981 --> 00:48:59,844
A few hundred thousand dollars?
Or a whole building?

607
00:49:00,633 --> 00:49:02,506
Keep it down, ma'am.

608
00:49:02,807 --> 00:49:05,920
One more shout and I'm calling the police.

609
00:49:10,027 --> 00:49:12,304
How much did she say she'd give you?

610
00:49:19,513 --> 00:49:20,880
Han Gyu Rim!

611
00:49:23,634 --> 00:49:25,607
Hey, can't you hear me?

612
00:49:25,632 --> 00:49:28,412
Hey! Excuse me! Hey!

613
00:49:28,561 --> 00:49:30,967
What did she say she'd give you?

614
00:49:31,633 --> 00:49:34,040
- I don't have a mother.
- What?

615
00:49:34,166 --> 00:49:36,196
My mother died a long time ago,

616
00:49:36,238 --> 00:49:40,506
so if you want to talk about yours,
go talk to your siblings, ma'am.

617
00:49:40,580 --> 00:49:42,726
Don't stand here yapping.

618
00:49:43,954 --> 00:49:46,194
Calling me "ma'am" every single time.

619
00:49:46,320 --> 00:49:48,120
You really know how to cut ties.

620
00:49:48,145 --> 00:49:53,458
Fine, if we're cutting ties,
let's cut them clean, Gyeol's mom.

621
00:49:53,678 --> 00:49:56,917
That's exactly what I want too,
Gyeol's mom.

622
00:49:57,235 --> 00:50:00,763
Just try saying hello
if we pass on the street, Gyeol's mom.

623
00:50:11,767 --> 00:50:15,282
If it ever comes out later
that Mom gave you anything,

624
00:50:15,410 --> 00:50:18,327
then I'm not staying quiet. I'll sue.

625
00:50:27,101 --> 00:50:30,684
She left a lunchbox. So what?

626
00:50:32,481 --> 00:50:36,717
She even wore sunglasses
so I wouldn't know she's my mother,

627
00:50:38,528 --> 00:50:42,287
and not after one year or two,

628
00:50:44,533 --> 00:50:46,632
but after 17 years, she shows up...

629
00:50:50,120 --> 00:50:52,632
A mother can't do that to her child.

630
00:50:54,247 --> 00:50:58,833
A mother isn't allowed to.

631
00:51:00,947 --> 00:51:02,637
She's still my mother,

632
00:51:04,305 --> 00:51:06,040
still my mother...

633
00:51:46,095 --> 00:51:48,632
This season's sports line keeps
the same functionality,

634
00:51:48,634 --> 00:51:52,865
but it's designed as lifewear
that works just as well every day.

635
00:51:55,601 --> 00:51:59,266
As you saw, we aimed for a wider
range of styles this fall,

636
00:51:59,291 --> 00:52:02,137
and we expect customer response
to be just as strong.

637
00:52:02,221 --> 00:52:05,113
And we've secured the inventory to match.

638
00:52:06,719 --> 00:52:10,251
To help every store
post strong results this season,

639
00:52:10,276 --> 00:52:13,275
we'll do our very best.
That concludes my presentation.

640
00:52:15,320 --> 00:52:17,518
Could I try this on just once?

641
00:52:24,735 --> 00:52:27,254
It's very good.

642
00:52:27,279 --> 00:52:30,483
- Please secure inventory on this one.
- Yes, understood.

643
00:52:30,508 --> 00:52:31,647
Us too.

644
00:52:34,990 --> 00:52:37,037
The response wasn't bad.

645
00:52:39,974 --> 00:52:41,490
I figured you'd drop work and everything,

646
00:52:41,522 --> 00:52:43,848
and go hole up somewhere...

647
00:52:44,680 --> 00:52:46,700
I can keep work and personal life apart.

648
00:52:47,134 --> 00:52:48,276
Really?

649
00:52:49,344 --> 00:52:51,197
Good thing you didn't get that from me.

650
00:52:51,801 --> 00:52:53,894
If there's nothing else, I'll be going.

651
00:52:55,034 --> 00:52:56,788
Your mother left home.

652
00:53:02,273 --> 00:53:03,853
I don't know where she is.

653
00:53:05,994 --> 00:53:08,572
Well, you walked out once,
and I walked out once,

654
00:53:08,597 --> 00:53:11,845
so it was only fair that your mother
got her turn to walk out.

655
00:53:15,313 --> 00:53:17,567
Are you two getting divorced?

656
00:53:18,713 --> 00:53:19,807
Who knows.

657
00:53:23,506 --> 00:53:26,281
I think your mother's considering it...

658
00:53:26,536 --> 00:53:27,653
I don't know.

659
00:53:29,640 --> 00:53:31,481
It isn't because of you.

660
00:53:33,747 --> 00:53:36,620
It won't come to that, but even if,
by some slim chance, it did,

661
00:53:36,645 --> 00:53:38,437
it wouldn't be because of you.

662
00:53:41,365 --> 00:53:44,678
Anyway, stop imposing on your friend,

663
00:53:45,623 --> 00:53:47,019
and come home.

664
00:53:49,853 --> 00:53:53,483
Seo Hyeon, I really don't know.

665
00:53:54,394 --> 00:53:57,780
What it means to be a parent, or a child.

666
00:54:05,326 --> 00:54:07,716
I'm heading out, so have the car ready.

667
00:54:08,993 --> 00:54:10,026
Dad.

668
00:54:11,833 --> 00:54:13,907
Write up the report
and submit it by tomorrow.

669
00:54:27,260 --> 00:54:28,926
Welcome.

670
00:54:35,480 --> 00:54:37,926
Drinking in broad daylight?

671
00:54:38,646 --> 00:54:41,319
You're here? Sit down.

672
00:54:45,840 --> 00:54:47,293
Thank you.

673
00:54:48,520 --> 00:54:50,512
Do you believe in fate and all that?

674
00:54:52,113 --> 00:54:54,049
I'm a total believer.

675
00:54:54,712 --> 00:54:55,740
Cheers.

676
00:54:58,861 --> 00:55:03,123
They told me there's a knife in my fate.

677
00:55:04,260 --> 00:55:08,149
That's why I cut my son off like that,

678
00:55:08,630 --> 00:55:11,928
and cut off a friend of 40 years.

679
00:55:11,953 --> 00:55:13,921
Same here.

680
00:55:14,454 --> 00:55:17,180
They said there are scissors
in my fate too,

681
00:55:17,254 --> 00:55:20,038
so everyone close to me
keeps cutting me off...

682
00:55:25,374 --> 00:55:27,743
Forty years,

683
00:55:28,397 --> 00:55:30,578
that's a friend you've had longer
than your son.

684
00:55:30,876 --> 00:55:33,192
Why cut him off completely?

685
00:55:35,694 --> 00:55:38,227
Because he kept talking absolute nonsense.

686
00:55:39,060 --> 00:55:40,928
Ruining his own life wasn't enough,

687
00:55:40,944 --> 00:55:44,694
so now that awful man is out to ruin
someone else's son's life too.

688
00:55:44,719 --> 00:55:47,580
How could he take his wife's daughter,

689
00:55:47,605 --> 00:55:50,082
and push her onto my son?

690
00:55:51,721 --> 00:55:54,987
If she's his wife's daughter,
isn't she his daughter?

691
00:55:58,274 --> 00:56:02,860
Anyway, the more I think about it,
the angrier I get.

692
00:56:05,821 --> 00:56:08,507
My son, my friend,

693
00:56:09,654 --> 00:56:13,655
how can they all do this to me?

694
00:56:13,786 --> 00:56:15,326
Are all men like this?

695
00:56:15,351 --> 00:56:18,504
Once they fall for a woman,
do they lose all common sense?

696
00:56:18,733 --> 00:56:21,733
Well, I've never had that experience.

697
00:56:22,600 --> 00:56:25,953
But I do understand that kind of betrayal.

698
00:56:26,347 --> 00:56:29,366
There's no part of my head left to stab.

699
00:56:29,767 --> 00:56:32,520
I've been betrayed and stabbed
in the back that many times.

700
00:56:32,954 --> 00:56:34,753
The guy I met in business,

701
00:56:34,981 --> 00:56:36,914
my son, and my friend. All of them.

702
00:56:45,693 --> 00:56:46,832
You know what?

703
00:56:48,028 --> 00:56:51,104
I know some guys
who will never betray you,

704
00:56:51,915 --> 00:56:53,306
so should I introduce you?

705
00:57:14,259 --> 00:57:15,537
Amazing!

706
00:57:17,067 --> 00:57:20,047
These guys will never betray you, ma'am.

707
00:57:20,072 --> 00:57:22,195
Anything else you like?

708
00:57:22,523 --> 00:57:23,900
How about that one? The pink one?

709
00:57:23,925 --> 00:57:26,504
What exactly do you do?

710
00:57:26,529 --> 00:57:30,243
Some people call me Santa Claus.

711
00:57:30,507 --> 00:57:32,610
You said your name was Seok Jung, right?

712
00:57:32,635 --> 00:57:34,608
You remembered.

713
00:57:34,633 --> 00:57:38,074
If we're going to be friends,
I should at least remember your name.

714
00:57:38,099 --> 00:57:39,625
Let's just be friends.

715
00:57:39,656 --> 00:57:42,440
Let's be friends.

716
00:57:42,465 --> 00:57:45,332
Two years apart,
so sure, let's be friends.

717
00:57:48,453 --> 00:57:51,908
- So what's your name, friend?
- Me?

718
00:57:56,975 --> 00:57:59,220
(Gyu Rim)

719
00:58:32,334 --> 00:58:34,674
(Gyu Rim)

720
00:58:34,699 --> 00:58:37,226
Is the trip going well?

721
00:58:37,494 --> 00:58:40,584
Are you eating properly?

722
00:58:41,201 --> 00:58:45,551
I hear it's warm by day and cold at night,
so be careful not to catch a cold.

723
00:58:52,454 --> 00:58:54,687
Nothing's wrong, is it?

724
00:58:55,482 --> 00:58:59,946
You never even liked trips,
and suddenly you're on one,

725
00:59:01,386 --> 00:59:04,806
so honestly, I'm worried.

726
00:59:06,400 --> 00:59:08,633
I'm afraid someone will come
and steal you away from me,

727
00:59:08,735 --> 00:59:11,968
that someone will show up
and claim you as their brother,

728
00:59:13,260 --> 00:59:15,080
and I'm really worried.

729
00:59:15,347 --> 00:59:16,847
That's 24 dollars.

730
00:59:16,867 --> 00:59:20,235
Even if a better, cooler sister shows up,

731
00:59:20,260 --> 00:59:24,945
and offers you snacks and bread,
don't waver for a second.

732
00:59:25,528 --> 00:59:30,102
Just come back home to me, quick,

733
00:59:30,621 --> 00:59:33,381
and run without looking back.

734
00:59:33,512 --> 00:59:39,991
I'll do better from now on, Gyu O.

735
00:59:54,160 --> 00:59:56,449
I'm sorry, Gyu Rim.

736
01:00:34,980 --> 01:00:36,403
Want me to fry you an egg?

737
01:00:39,261 --> 01:00:40,801
Hey, slow down.

738
01:00:40,826 --> 01:00:42,326
I'm not taking any.

739
01:00:46,941 --> 01:00:48,409
I'm not going to die.

740
01:00:49,320 --> 01:00:50,673
I'm going to live.

741
01:00:51,814 --> 01:00:53,200
Who said otherwise?

742
01:00:57,640 --> 01:00:59,326
I'm never going to die.

743
01:00:59,492 --> 01:01:00,847
Not even if it kills me.

744
01:01:03,513 --> 01:01:05,486
Hey, but I'm starving.

745
01:01:05,794 --> 01:01:07,233
You didn't eat it all, did you?

746
01:01:07,394 --> 01:01:09,133
- I ate it all.
- What?

747
01:01:14,088 --> 01:01:15,925
- Hey.
- There's none in there.

748
01:01:23,961 --> 01:01:25,047
Gyu Rim.

749
01:01:29,424 --> 01:01:30,985
Gyu Min said you went to Namhae,

750
01:01:30,999 --> 01:01:33,321
and that you'd be back in a week.

751
01:01:34,207 --> 01:01:36,167
I was going to come back in a week,

752
01:01:36,440 --> 01:01:39,756
but some weird sister showed up
offering me snacks and bread,

753
01:01:39,975 --> 01:01:41,964
trying to talk me into being her brother.

754
01:01:42,574 --> 01:01:44,180
You said to come back quick, right?

755
01:01:44,205 --> 01:01:46,012
To run without looking back?

756
01:01:48,146 --> 01:01:49,834
So I ran like crazy.

757
01:01:53,647 --> 01:01:55,220
What happened to your face?

758
01:01:56,493 --> 01:01:58,274
Where did you get hurt?

759
01:01:58,656 --> 01:02:00,394
Who did this?

760
01:02:05,788 --> 01:02:07,782
Something happened, didn't it?

761
01:02:11,300 --> 01:02:13,072
A lot of things happened.

762
01:02:14,447 --> 01:02:18,240
What? What happened?

763
01:02:20,294 --> 01:02:22,594
It's too long to tell right now.

764
01:02:23,539 --> 01:02:26,886
I'm dead tired,
too tired to say a single word.

765
01:02:31,286 --> 01:02:34,255
- Gyu O.
- Not today. At your 100th birthday,

766
01:02:35,633 --> 01:02:37,427
can I answer you then?

767
01:02:50,540 --> 01:02:51,801
You can.

768
01:02:53,274 --> 01:02:54,667
That's all right.

769
01:02:56,512 --> 01:03:00,672
I'll have to live a really long time
to hear your answer, won't I?

770
01:03:04,406 --> 01:03:06,419
You came back. That's enough.

771
01:03:08,654 --> 01:03:12,668
You came back safe. That's enough.

772
01:03:15,307 --> 01:03:17,311
This is enough for me, Gyu O.

773
01:03:20,666 --> 01:03:24,827
You went through a lot. Welcome home.

774
01:04:27,032 --> 01:04:29,825
(Love on the Menu)

775
01:04:29,860 --> 01:04:31,846
Give up on my brother, Ms. Kwon.

776
01:04:31,947 --> 01:04:33,842
Weren't you the one who said
never give up?

777
01:04:33,867 --> 01:04:35,602
But he won't give up.

778
01:04:35,627 --> 01:04:37,807
I think I got tricked into this marriage.

779
01:04:37,827 --> 01:04:39,080
You're the one who did the tricking.

780
01:04:39,120 --> 01:04:42,167
If mom and dad get divorced,
is it because of me?

781
01:04:42,192 --> 01:04:45,166
When did you get so thoughtful?

782
01:04:45,241 --> 01:04:48,515
Could you tell me a way
to make him run away from me?

783
01:04:48,547 --> 01:04:49,980
I'm going to look into it myself.

784
01:04:50,005 --> 01:04:52,894
Whether I should give him my blessing,
or put a stop to it.

785
01:04:52,919 --> 01:04:54,432
I really want to be happy today.

786
01:04:54,457 --> 01:04:57,459
Let's go all the way
and see what becomes of us.

787
01:04:58,540 --> 01:05:00,340
Dramaday.me
